{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14527 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Neomycin is implicated in the interaction with A549 cells through a series of molecular pathways involving melanocyte proteins. The evidence suggests that neomycin targets the Melanocyte protein PMEL, which is a common target for multiple compounds, including L-Radicamine A, 9-Hydroxy-10,12,15-octadecatrienoic acid, and 4-Methoxy-1-benzofuran-5-carboxylic acid. These compounds, in turn, have a target of A549, indicating a potential mechanism by which neomycin may exert its effects on the cell line. The shared targeting of PMEL across these compounds suggests a possible functional relationship, possibly involving the modulation of melanocyte-related pathways. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of PMEL in mediating the interaction between neomycin and A549, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
